acceptance_criteria: "Built hassio exposes a typed bounded bootstrap integration observation command with deterministic summaries, validation, auto-unsubscribe cleanup, detailed help, schema, capabilities, and all six output formats; Non-interactive settings wizard stdout is exactly one valid TOON, JSON, JSON-compact, YAML, table, or Markdown receipt and connection failures are represented deterministically without leaking secrets; Isolated setup writes secure settings/auth/data files; live read-only startup acceptance retains only redacted counts, booleans, versions, and field names; Build, typecheck, lint, docstrings, duplication, file-size, ShellCheck, audit, Trivy, PM/changelog, release dry-run, package smoke, help E2E, and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage pass"
definition_of_ready: All 85 PM items and 364 graph edges inspected; duplicate scan and exact semantic searches completed; latest pm-cli and pm-changelog 2026.8.7 confirmed; official Core 2026.8.1 and current developer docs inspected; live Core 2026.7.4 and isolated wizard defect reproduced without persisting private output
goal: agent-native-home-assistant-operations
objective: typed-startup-readiness-and-machine-safe-setup
value: Agents and operators can diagnose slow or incomplete startup and bootstrap a secure CLI configuration without raw protocol handling or fragile stdout parsing.
impact: "Improves startup observability, CI automation safety, and forward-compatible API completeness while preserving a strict privacy boundary."
outcome: "A production-ready startup readiness and setup flow with typed contracts, exact tests, complete docs, and hosted review proof."
why_now: "Core 2026.8.1 exposes one stable core subscription not yet typed by the CLI, and live isolated acceptance found that the mandatory wizard corrupts JSON output with human banners."
